Show images, video and audio inline in the chat, lay images in a row out as
a grid, and let the lightbox pinch-zoom and page through them.

Upstream renders markdown images with Streamdown's harden pass set to allow
no image prefixes, so every `![alt](…)` became "[Image blocked: alt]", and a
workspace path could never load anyway: the file lives in the sandbox.

- An image that names a workspace file (absolute, relative or `file:`) is
  moved off `src` before harden (markWorkspaceMedia) and loaded through the
  filesystem API's raw download as a Blob (fetchWorkspaceFileBlob), which
  works in the native shells and lets Safari play a video the endpoint can't
  serve with range requests. https and data images render as written; plain
  http stays blocked (blockPlainHttpImages), so an agent can't make the
  viewer's browser send requests to devices on their own network.
- A path or URL ending in a video or audio extension plays in a native
  player (ChatMarkdownMedia, lib/mediaKind).
- Two or more images separated only by whitespace or blank lines become one
  grid (groupMediaGalleries). Streamdown parses each block alone, so
  parseMarkdownIntoMediaBlocks keeps a run of image-only blocks together.
- The shared lightbox (ImageLightbox) zooms with a two-finger pinch on a
  touch screen, double-tap, and a wheel or trackpad pinch at the cursor;
  keeps a zoomed image within its edges; pages through a grid's images, and
  a user message's attachments, with arrows, the arrow keys or a swipe; and
  closes with a downward swipe.
- A loaded file stays in memory with the message that showed it
  (lib/chatMediaCache), so the chat doesn't flash. It remounts a message's
  media when a streamed reply is saved and when you come back to a session,
  and each mount would download the file again behind a spinner. BubbleView
  provides the bubble's stable key as ChatMediaScope, and a remount paints
  the version the message showed in its first frame, without a download. A
  message showing a path for the first time fetches it, so a reply showing a
  file the agent overwrote shows the new version; mounts while a download is
  in flight, or within a second of it, share it. An image is decoded before
  it replaces its spinner. A file that failed stays a chip, retried in the
  background after 10 seconds. Object URLs nothing shows are revoked past
  300 files or 192 MiB.

Upstream's two tests that remote images stay blocked now check that https
renders and plain http doesn't.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0032.
